  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Early Career Researchers</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">INASP is an international organization that works to strengthen research and knowledge systems in the Global South. Through the program &#x201c;Equipping early career researchers to succeed,&#x201d; INASP will enhance research capacity at NORHED universities. This will be achieved through digital and hybrid learning programs, as well as establishing institutional partnerships with three selected NORHED institutions in Sub-Saharan Africa. The goal is for universities and the new generation of researchers to be able to conduct high-quality, relevant research addressing social, environmental, and developmental challenges. INASP will also proactively address women&apos;s rights by embedding gender equality across the project to ensure that learning programs are gender responsive. Additionally, collaboration with three partner universities will specifically focus on addressing gender and inclusion.</narrative>
  </description>
